A||||11||RadRuss||what is the best V8 engine swap?||||5||
Z||000000||RadRuss||10-27-2001||03:37 PM||||ok, i am going to do an engine swap soon and i am looking for some thing that has alot of balls to it. i see everyone putting this and that into their cars and i was wondering what engine is the best for speed and fairly easy to put in? like not much rear end modification to fit it in. can u guys help me out? <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signiturecar_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||TRiAD||10-27-2001||04:04 PM||||This may not be what you were looking for, but they aren't cheap, and do take a LOT of modification to fit. <P>That said, have Archie put an LT1 in it and never look back.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jim_Sprang||10-27-2001||04:39 PM||||I have had a SBC in mine since 94, first a number of 350s now a 406.  I think bang for the buck the small block chev conversion can't be beat.  But there are a lot more costs than what appear at first glance.  Having said that I have had mine together for 7 years and still love the car and the conversion.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||10-27-2001||04:39 PM||||Caddy 4.9ltr Motor is cheap. Autocrosser Greg Duncan sells flywheels for the conversion for $400 and from the sounds of it , it's the easiest V8 swap there is. And it adds no weight to the Fiero.<P>Downside...No performance parts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Limited HP in comparison to a 350<P>upside lotsa TQ, cheap motor , bolts up to the Fiero tranny , sounds good (like a smallblock) cheap cheap cheap. I saw a motor in last nights paper for $400 candian with 80,000 miles on it. ad says runs great.<P>Personally I would love a 350 , but the caddy 4. X series of motors seems to be catching on quite a bit<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay||10-27-2001||07:55 PM||||I've got the Northstar and love it!  Electronics are not as bad as people say.  Check my site for info.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||10-27-2001||08:07 PM||||Until someone does a Northstar kit that you can buy, the easiest is the regular Small Block Chevy.  Mainly because you just write Archie a check and you get all parts and tech support necessary to do the job.  And with a SBC, HP is limited only by your wallet.<P>I'd prefer the N*, but until someone offers a tried and true kit for one, I'd stick with the SBC. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||northstarfieroorbust||10-27-2001||09:21 PM||||there is a northstar kit availible through <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com</A> <BR>im looking at getting it myself actually||||reg||1
